ystone State Park that passes a wetland, meadow, and pine forest.","source_url":"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/keystone-state-park/hiking","source_title":"Hiking at Keystone State Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Pennsylvania state parks do not charge an entrance fee; remain on the designated trail.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"keystone-wildlife-watching","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Keystone State Park Wildlife Watching","title":"Watch for Migrating Birds","subtitle":"Keystone State Park, near Latrobe","notes":"Bring binoculars if you have them, scan quietly from established areas, and observe wildlife without approaching or handling any animals.","short_summary":"A seasonal bird-and-wildlife observation outing around Keystone’s lake and habitats.","evidence_claim":"Keystone State Park reports that warblers, kinglets, buffleheads, mergansers, herons, osprey, and other birds migrate through the park.","source_url":"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/keystone-state-park/wildlife-watching","source_title":"Wildlife Watching at Keystone State Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Pennsylvania state parks do not charge an entrance fee; observe animals from a distance and do not handle them.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"laurel-highlands-hiking-trail","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Laurel Highlands Hiking Trail","title":"Day Hike the Laurel Highlands Trail","subtitle":"Laurel Ridge State Park","notes":"Pick a daylight section from a designated trailhead, share the route with the group, and use the voluntary day-use registration mailbox.","short_summary":"A choose-your-distance day hike on Laurel Ridge’s long-distance trail.","evidence_claim":"Laurel Ridge State Park’s main feature is the 70-mile Laurel Highlands Hiking Trail; day hikers are asked to use voluntary registration mailboxes at trailheads.","source_url":"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/laurel-ridge-state-park/stay","source_title":"Stay the Night at Laurel Ridge State Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Pennsylvania state parks do not charge an entrance fee. This card is for day hiking only; overnight use requires a reservation and fee.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"adams-falls-trail","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Adams Falls Trail","title":"See Adams Falls","subtitle":"Linn Run State Park","notes":"Walk the one-mile loop with friends, stay on the designated route near the waterfall, and leave time to return before dusk.","short_summary":"A short state-park waterfall walk through rhododendron and hemlock.","evidence_claim":"DCNR describes Adams Falls Trail at Linn Run State Park as a one-mile loop leading to a mountain waterfall among rhododendron and hemlock.","source_url":"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/scenic-features/pa-waterfalls","source_title":"Waterfalls in Pennsylvania State Parks","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Pennsylvania state parks do not charge an entrance fee; use care around water and remain on the marked trail.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"winnie-palmer-wetland-boardwalk","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Wetland Boardwalk","title":"Visit the Wetland Boardwalk","subtitle":"Winnie Palmer Nature Reserve, Saint Vincent College","notes":"Meet at the reserve and take a slow boardwalk lap to look for marsh birds and native plants; respect the habitat and posted rules.","short_summary":"A campus-adjacent marsh boardwalk for a low-key nature walk.","evidence_claim":"Winnie Palmer Nature Reserve identifies its Wetland Boardwalk as a place to see native marshes, red-winged blackbirds, cattails, and jewelweed.","source_url":"https://www.wpnr.org/","source_title":"Winnie Palmer Nature Reserve","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The reserve lists trail hours as daily dawn to dusk and does not list an admission charge for visiting its trails.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
